 "limits_and_declared_deviations": [
  "no engine invariant was relaxed: cash >= 0, deployed <= C0, per-side friction, the ADD cap, forced flat and the exit-carry rules are untouched",
  "a scheduled NEW entry never carries into a later session (unlike a pending EXIT, \u00a76): it is cancelled at the session end, counted in buy_side.n_entry_unfilled and flagged",
  "when a hook is declared, the day's candidate bars join the event grid, so deployed_avg for an extension run is sampled on that grid (no existing run moves)",
  "new entries are full slot budgets or nothing; after a stop-out a re-entry may be unfunded and is then skipped (counted once per day)",
  "the unfunded/capped counters count (day, hook, kind) once, not once per scanned bar",
  "re-entry is same-session only, and mid/re-entry candidates come only from the entry snapshot's top_n",
  "resume validation widened to (sleeve_day, ticker, entry_et) because a sleeve day can now hold two tickets for one name (entry + re-entry) - see D_resume_probe",
  "the EXT-1 fingerprint gap is closed in the same change: batch_policy is now bound (documented in EXTENSIONS.md EXT-1 item 6)",
  "not verified here: EXT-1 batch_policy together with EXT-2 hooks in one cell (call sites are independent; no canary run declares both)"
 ],
